# The lantern's reactions to things you do, said in speech bubbles beside
# him. Each section is one thing he might say, tagged with the moment it's
# for: the game says "caught" when you land a fish, and he says one of the
# caught sections (never the same one twice running, if there's another).
# See scripts/dialogue/remark.gd for the tags and guards a section can have.
#
# Moments: returned, remembered, caught, morning, hove_to, supper, dim,
# far_light, island, pulled_out, fog_cleared.
# Placeholder writing: rewrite freely.

# (His first words, the night he pulled you from the sea, are in the opening
# cutscene: intro.dlg.)

# You've come back to a saved voyage.
~ returned_1 [on returned]
lantern: You're back. I kept the light on.

~ returned_2 [on returned]
lantern: There you are again.
lantern: I didn't go anywhere. I can't, really.

# A memory of home has just come back.
~ remembered_1 [on remembered]
lantern: Was that home? It sounded like home.

~ remembered_2 [on remembered]
lantern: Oh! Say it again. Slower.

~ remembered_3 [on remembered]
lantern: I think I remember that too. I don't. But I'd like to.

~ remembered_4 [on remembered]
lantern: Hold on to that one.

# You've landed a fish.
~ caught_1 [on caught]
lantern: A fish! Is home a fish? ...No. Probably not. [shout]

~ caught_2 [on caught]
lantern: That one looked like it knew the way.

~ caught_3 [on caught]
lantern: Supper! I'll watch. I'm very good at watching.

# You've woken at dawn.
~ morning_1 [on morning]
lantern: Morning! Did you sleep? I don't. I just glow quieter.

~ morning_2 [on morning]
lantern: The rain's tired too, I think.

~ morning_3 [on morning]
lantern: Look, it's grey and pink. That's my favourite colour.

# You've stopped the ship at the bell.
~ hove_to_1 [on hove_to]
lantern: Stopping? Good. I like it when the sea holds still.

~ hove_to_2 [on hove_to]
lantern: The fish will come now. Fish like quiet.

# You've shared a meal with him.
~ supper_1 [on supper]
lantern: Oh, that's warm all the way through.

~ supper_2 [on supper]
lantern: Mm. Tastes like a Tuesday. A good one.

~ supper_3 [on supper]
lantern: I'm glowing. Am I glowing? I'm glowing.

~ supper_4 [on supper]
lantern: You cook like someone who's been missed.

# His warmth is running low.
~ dim_1 [on dim]
lantern: I'm a bit... dim. Is there soup?

~ dim_2 [on dim]
lantern: Is it me, or is it darker in here? It's me, isn't it. [thought]

# You're at the bow at night, looking towards the far light.
~ far_light_1 [on far_light]
lantern: A light! That's it. That's home. Probably. Almost certainly. Maybe. [shout]

~ far_light_2 [on far_light]
lantern: If it isn't home, it's very good at pretending.

~ far_light_3 [on far_light]
lantern: Somebody's keeping that light lit. For somebody.

# You're at the bow at dawn, and the island has come out of the mist.
~ island_1 [on island]
lantern: There! An island. With a lighthouse. Lighthouses are for people who are lost. So, us.

~ island_2 [on island]
lantern: That's where the light lives. I knew it. I didn't, but I knew it.

~ island_3 [on island]
lantern: Do you think it remembers you? Islands are very good at remembering.

# A fog-touched creature has beaten you, and he's pulled you back to the landing.
~ pulled_out_1 [on pulled_out]
lantern: Got you! I've got you. You dropped some things. I didn't count.

~ pulled_out_2 [on pulled_out]
lantern: Up you come. It didn't mean it. It's the fog that pinches.

~ pulled_out_3 [on pulled_out]
lantern: That's twice I've pulled you out of somewhere. I'm keeping score. Kindly.

# You've cleared the fog from a creature.
~ fog_cleared_1 [on fog_cleared]
lantern: Look at it go! It only wanted its head clear. [shout]

~ fog_cleared_2 [on fog_cleared]
lantern: There. All shaken off. It'll remember being a crab now.

~ fog_cleared_3 [on fog_cleared]
lantern: Oh, well done. Gently done.
